  "body": "## What changed (slice 2 of 3: app)\n\nStacked on #1101 (slice 1), which stacks on #945. Fork synced at v0.18.0. Effort: high.\n\nThe app now hands the post the setup's 1-based work-offset index, not a word. The setup's own post sets the limit; core keeps only a sanity bound.\n\n- **The stream carries the index.** `camcraft_post::post::Dump::wcs` is now a `u32`, where 1 is the first offset. `posting::wcs_context` returns `(index, origin)`. The post writes the word.\n- **No fallback (triage point 2).** `setup::work_offset` no longer filters the stored pick. If a setup's post cannot express the stored offset, the offset is still never read as offset 1 or G54. That holds for the stream, the travel check, the label and the setup sheet.\n- **Post-time gate.** New `setup_offsets::range_problems`, part of `verification_report`, so it applies to the single-file, per-mount and per-op posts. It checks each setup that has an operation against that setup's own post (`setup_mount::post_of`). An offset the post cannot express blocks the post, naming the setup and the post. Slice 1's engine refusal still runs behind it.\n- **Command-time check.** `SetSetupWorkOffset::new` checks the pick against the setup's post (`setup_offsets::check`) and refuses by name.\n- **Loader.** The six-offset cap is removed from `project/apply.rs`. Only the sanity bound remains (pick 0..=254, the `u8` that the height digest stores).\n- **Names.** New `setup::work_offset_names(world, setup)` reads slice 1's `work_offsets(cps)` table. It is cached per (resolved post, script text) in a bounded map. `setup::offset_name`, `setup::wcs_name` and `setup::wcs_label` use it, and so do the setup sheet, the refusal texts, the spindle-law text and the shared-offset clause. The names are for display only and never go into the stream.\n- **File format.** Offsets 1-6 are still saved as `G54`..`G59`, so existing files round-trip byte-identical. Offsets 7 and up are saved as their number. **Builds older than this one cannot open a file that uses offset 7 or higher.** The decision file records this for the release notes (point 8).\n- **`WCS_SLOTS` is split (point 1).** It is now a crate-private `LEGACY_WCS_NAMES`, used only for legacy entity-name reservations and the pre-v52 and pre-v54 migrations. All of its word uses are gone.\n- **`shared_word_problems` (point 7)** compares offset indexes and names the offset by the post's name.\n- **UI and MCP** keep working through the app functions. The Setups combo still lists offsets 1-6, now named by the setup's post. MCP still accepts the words G54-G59. Slice 3 changes the combo and adds MCP's `index`.\n\n## How tested\n\n- Pinning tests in `crates/app/tests/wcs_index.rs`:\n  - `offset_nine_on_a_six_offset_post_refuses_by_setup_name_and_never_posts_at_offset_one` (the no-fallback pin)\n  - `the_command_refuses_an_offset_the_setups_post_cannot_express`\n  - `the_setups_post_names_its_offsets`\n  - `offset_seven_and_up_saves_as_its_number_and_reloads`\n- Unit test: `project::wcs_pick::tests::legacy_words_and_numbers_round_trip`.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` is green on 671ccd19: post suites, about 250 app suites including `wcs_index`, `setup_wcs`, `posting`, `probe_*`, `project_roundtrip` and `conformance`, the ui lib plus 11 ui suites. Wall time 9.6 min.\n- I also ran 23 golden and post suites that the quick gate does not pick, including `golden_cl`, `carvera_post`, `heidenhain_*`, `tormach_post` and `lathe_post_*`. All pass, and no golden file changed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No GUI hand check and no Hub run. The combo is unchanged apart from where its names come from.\n- A user `.cps` file post with extended offsets was not tried by hand. It goes through the same cache path as the built-in posts.\n\nWaits on #1101's Hub run. Like #1101, it merges at the next cut.\n\nDecisions: `docs/decisions/931-wcs-index-app.md`.\n\nChangelog: Work offsets are an index whose limit and names come from each setup's post. An offset the post cannot express is refused by setup name instead of posting at G54. Offsets 7 and up are saved as their number, and older builds cannot open those files. (#931)\n\nRefs #931\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n",
